{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"The_Maw","to":"The Maw"},{"from":"Fungi_Beast","to":"Fungi Beast"},{"from":"Orb_Walker","to":"Orb Walker"},{"from":"The_Champ","to":"The Champ"}],"pages":{"2433":{"pageid":2433,"ns":0,"title":"Fungi Beast","revisions":[{"revid":55796,"parentid":53439,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Fungi Beast\n|Image  = FungiBeast.png\n|HP     = 22-28\n|AscHP  = 24-28\n|Powers = {{BD|Spore Cloud}} 2\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Spore Cloud}}\n'''Fungi Beast''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that appears in [[Act 1]] and [[Act 2]]. It also appears in the {{E|Hypnotizing Colored Mushrooms}} [[Event]] in groups of three.\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Fungi Beast}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Bite\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals 6 damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Grow\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = Gains (3;{{Asc|2|4}} ; {{Asc|17|5}}) {{BD|Strength}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Fungi Beast''' will use one of the following attacks each turn:\n* {{Int|Fungi Beast|Bite}} (60% chance)\n* {{Int|Fungi Beast|Grow}} (40% chance)\n'''Fungi Beast''' will not use {{Int|Fungi Beast|Bite}} 3 times in a row or {{Int|Fungi Beast|Grow}} twice in a row.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 1 ===\nAs a hard pool encounter alongside:\n* 1 other {{M|Fungi Beast}}\n\nAs half of the Exordium Wildlife encounter along with either:\n* 1 {{M|Green Louse}} or {{M|Red Louse}}\n* 1 {{M|Acid Slime (M)}} or {{M|Spike Slime (M)}}\n\nIn the {{E|Hypnotizing Colored Mushrooms}} [[Event]] alongside:\n* 2 other {{M|Fungi Beast|Fungi Beasts}}\n\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs a hard pool encounter alongside:\n* 1 {{M|Shelled Parasite}}\n\n== Tips ==\n* {{BD|Spore Cloud}} will still activate even if a '''Fungi Beast''' is killed during the enemy's turn (ex. from {{BD|Thorns}} damage). Make sure to keep that in mind to avoid the extra damage other enemies may inflict while you have {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* '''Fungi Beasts''' appear to be [[Slay the Spire 2:Two-Tailed Rat|Two-tailed Rats]] infested with a parasitic fungus.\n** {{M|Gremlin Nob}} wields a similar rodent-like skeleton as a weapon, presumably belonging to the same enemy.\n\n== Update History ==\n* Weekly Patch 38: Bane\n** Parasite + Fungi Beast combat can actually be encountered now.\n\n* Weekly Patch 37: Darkness\n** New City Encounter - Shelled Parasite and Fungi Beast.\n\n* Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life\n** We updated the animations for several monsters! Affected monsters include: Fungi Beasts\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"2513":{"pageid":2513,"ns":0,"title":"Orb Walker","revisions":[{"revid":56104,"parentid":55879,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Under Construction}}{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Orb Walker\n|Image  = OrbWalker.png\n|HP     = 90-96\n|AscHP  = 92-102\n|Powers = {{BD|Strength Up}} 3 ({{Asc|17|5}})\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Normal\n}} {{Power Infobox|Strength Up}}\n'''Orb Walker''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 3]]. It can also be encountered in the {{E|Mysterious Sphere}} [[Event]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Orb Walker}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Laser\n|Intent = DebuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|11}}) damage. Adds a {{C|Burn}} into your draw pile, and another {{C|Burn}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Claw\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (15;{{Asc|2|16}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Orb Walker''' will use one of the following actions each turn:\n* {{Int|Orb Walker|Laser}} (60% chance)\n* {{Int|Orb Walker|Claw}} (40% chance)\n'''Orb Walker''' cannot use either action three times in a row.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 3 ===\nAs an easy pool encounter:\n* Solo\n\nIn the {{E|Mysterious Sphere}} [[Event]] alongside:\n* 1 other '''Orb Walker'''\n\n== Tips ==\n\n* The Orb Walker scales strength somewhat quickly, with the added threat of diluting your draw pile with [[Burn|Burns]]. End the fight quickly and, if necessary, consider taking damage in early turns to play critical cards.\n* {{BD|Weak}} is effective at blocking large amounts of damage if the fight is drawn out.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* '''Orb Walker''' appears in the artwork of {{C|Evaluate}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act\n** Awakened One and Orb Walkers were not shuffling their status cards into the player's draw pile, but into a fixed position.\n\n* Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline\n** Double Orb Walker elite encounter removed from the game.\n** The Mysterious Sphere event in Act 3 now uses the Double Orb Walker combat.\n\n* Weekly Patch 25: Building Blocks\n** Mysterious Sphere event enemies now attack in the correct order\n\n* Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face\n** Fixed issue where Shield Gremlin and Orb Walker had upped values in the wrong Ascension Level.\n\n* Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life\n** We updated the animations for several monsters! Affected monsters include: Orb Walkers\n\n* Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!\n** For the 2 Orb Walker encounter they now attack left -> right.\n\n* Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!\n** Double Orb Walkers migrate to the elite pool.\n\n* Day 1 Patch\n** Updating y position of orb walker for dual Orb Walkers combat.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"3051":{"pageid":3051,"ns":0,"title":"Shapes","revisions":[{"revid":55770,"parentid":53495,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"The Shapes are a group of enemies encountered in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Exploder ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Exploder\n|Image  = Exploder.png\n|HP     = 30\n|AscHP  = 30-35\n|Powers = {{BD|Explosive}} 3\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Explosive}}\nExploders explode. Profound knowledge.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Exploder}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Attack\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals (9;{{Asc|2|11}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Explode\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Deals 30 damage. Dies.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nAlways uses this pattern:\n* {{Int|Exploder|Attack}}\n* {{Int|Exploder|Attack}}\n* {{Int|Exploder|Explode}}\n\n{{Clear}}\n== Repulsor ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Repulsor\n|Image  = Repulsor.png\n|HP     = 29-35\n|AscHP  = 31-38\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Dazed}}\nRepulsor repeatedly gives the player {{C|Dazed}}.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Repulsor}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Daze\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Adds 2 {{C|Dazed}} into your draw pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Attack\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (11;{{Asc|2|13}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''On all turns:'''\n* {{Int|Repulsor|Attack}} 20% chance\n* {{Int|Repulsor|Daze}} 80% chance\n\nCannot use {{Int|Repulsor|Attack}} twice in a row.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Spiker ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spiker\n|Image  = Spiker.png\n|HP     = 42-56\n|AscHP  = 44-60\n|Powers = {{BD|Thorns}} 3 ({{Asc|2|4}} {{!}} {{Asc|17|7}})\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Thorns}}\nSpikers focus on building up {{BD|Thorns}} to make them more dangerous to kill as the battle progresses.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Spiker}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Attack\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals (7;{{Asc|2|9}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Buff Thorns\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = Gains 2 {{BD|Thorns}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nOn every turn, it has a 50/50 chance of using either {{Int|Spiker|Attack}} or {{Int|Spiker|Buff Thorns}}.\n\nCannot use {{Int|Spiker|Attack}} twice in a row. Cannot use {{Int|Spiker|Buff Thorns}} once it has been used 6 times and will instead using {{Int|Spiker|Attack}}.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Found With ==\n=== Act 3 ===\nIn the Easy Pool's '''3 Shapes''' encounter with:\n* Three random Shapes (No more than two of the same shape)\n\nIn the Hard Pool's '''4 Shapes''' encounter with:\n* Four random Shapes (No more than two of the same shape)\n\nIn the '''Spheric Guardian''' encounter with:\n* {{M|Spheric Guardian}}\n* Two random Shapes\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"3027":{"pageid":3027,"ns":0,"title":"The Champ","revisions":[{"revid":55686,"parentid":53488,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = The Champ\n|Image  = Champ.png\n|Icon   = Map-Champ.png\n|HP     = 420\n|AscHP  = 440\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Boss\n}}\nThe Champ is a [[Boss]] found at the end of [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|The Champ}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Heavy Slash\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (16;{{Asc|4|18}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Face Slap\n|Intent = DebuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (12;{{Asc|4|14}}) damage. Applies 2 {{BD|Frail}} and 2 {{BD|Vulnerable}}}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Defensive Stance\n|Intent = DefendBuff\n|Effect = Gains (15;{{Asc|9|18}} ; {{Asc|19|20}}) {{KW|Block}} and (5;{{Asc|9|6}} ; {{Asc|19|7}}) {{BD|Metallicize}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Gloat\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = Gains (2;{{Asc|4|3}} ; {{Asc|19|4}}) {{BD|Strength}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Taunt\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Applies 2 {{BD|Weak}} and 2 {{BD|Vulnerable}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Anger\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = Removes all [[Debuffs]]. Gains (6;{{Asc|4|9}} ; {{Asc|19|12}}) {{BD|Strength}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Execute\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals 10\u00d72 damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n=== Phase One ===\nAlways uses {{Int|The Champ|Taunt}} every 4 turns.\n\n'''On all other turns:'''\n* {{Int|The Champ|Defensive Stance}} 15% chance\n* {{Int|The Champ|Gloat}} ({{Int|The Champ|Defensive Stance}} {{Asc|19}}) 15% chance\n* {{Int|The Champ|Face Slap}} 25% chance\n* {{Int|The Champ|Heavy Slash}} 45% chance\n\nNo move can be used twice in a row.\n\nOn {{Asc|19|Ascension}}, when {{Int|The Champ|Gloat}} is replaced with {{Int|The Champ|Defensive Stance}}, if the last move was also {{Int|The Champ|Defensive Stance}}, he will instead use {{Int|The Champ|Gloat}}.\n\n=== Phase Two ===\nWhen his HP drops below 50%, he will use {{Int|The Champ|Anger}} on the next turn and enter Phase Two.\n\nAfter using {{Int|The Champ|Anger}} he will use {{Int|The Champ|Execute}} the turn after.\n\nHe will then repeat this pattern for the rest of combat:\n* Random Move (Same chances as Phase One)\n* Random Move (Same chances as Phase One)\n* {{Int|The Champ|Execute}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The Champ appears in the artwork of {{C|Pressure Points}} and {{C|Wheel Kick}}.\n* The {{R|Champion Belt}} Relic belongs to the Champ. If you fight him with it obtained, he will scream \"{{TS||shake|THAT'S MY BELT!!}}\" on his first turn.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Bosses]]"}}}]},"3052":{"pageid":3052,"ns":0,"title":"The Maw","revisions":[{"revid":55976,"parentid":53498,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = The Maw\n|Image  = Maw.png\n|HP     = 300\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\nThe Maw is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|The Maw}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Roar\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Applies (3;{{Asc|17|5}}) {{BD|Weak}} and (3;{{Asc|17|5}}) {{BD|Frail}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Slam\n|Intent = Attack6\n|Effect = Deals (25;{{Asc|2|30}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Nom Nom\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals 5\u00d7N damage. N = Current turn, divided by two (rounded up).}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Drool\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = Gains (3;{{Asc|17|5}}) {{BD|Strength}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nAlways starts with {{Int|The Maw|Roar}}. Afterwards it has a 50/50 chance of using either {{Int|The Maw|Slam}} or {{Int|The Maw|Nom Nom}}.\n\n'''After using {{Int|The Maw|Drool}}:''' 50/50 split between {{Int|The Maw|Slam}} and {{Int|The Maw|Nom Nom}}.\n\n'''After using {{Int|The Maw|Slam}}:''' 50/50 split between {{Int|The Maw|Nom Nom}} and {{Int|The Maw|Drool}}.\n\n'''After using {{Int|The Maw|Nom Nom}}:''' Always uses {{Int|The Maw|Drool}}.\n\n== Found With ==\n=== Act 3 ===\n* Solo\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The Maw is the only enemy whose Max HP does not change based on [[Ascension]] level.\n* The Maw appears in the artwork of {{C|Weave}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]}}}}